---
title: Lying Dumbbell Svend Press
type: docs
prev: docs/grud/
---
![](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/191448d7-c521-48ed-9241-9c75e634e557)


{{% steps %}}

### Step 1
Grab the dumbbells and lie on a flat bench. Keep a natural slight arch in your lower back, pull your shoulders down away from your ears, and squeeze your shoulder blades together.

### Step 2
Hold the dumbbells up over your chest and press them firmly against each other, palms facing in. Point your elbows out to the sides.

### Step 3
Inhale and slowly lower the dumbbells down to your chest while keeping them pressed together and flaring your elbows out.

### Step 4
Touch the dumbbells lightly to your chest, then exhale and slowly press them back up to the starting position.

{{% /steps %}}

{{< callout type="info" >}}
• Do not use momentum—perform the movement slowly and with full control.

• Keep the dumbbells moving in a straight vertical line with your elbows pointed out to the sides.

• Keep your breathing smooth and steady.
{{< /callout >}}
